CowSwapModuleFactory_CreateDeterministic
├── when the caller is neither the factory owner nor an approved operator
│   ├── it should revert with CowSwapModuleFactory_NotOwnerOrOperator
│   └── it should leave the predicted address unoccupied
├── when the caller is an approved operator
│   └── it should deploy to the predicted address
├── when the caller is a revoked operator
│   └── it should revert with CowSwapModuleFactory_NotOwnerOrOperator
├── when the owner deployed the same args and salt as an approved operator first
│   └── it should revert, leaving the shared contract at the predicted address
├── when owner is zero address
│   └── it should revert with CowSwapModuleFactory_ZeroOwner
├── when paymentRails is zero address
│   └── it should revert with CowSwapModuleFactory_ZeroPaymentRails
├── when paymentRails has no code
│   └── it should revert with CowSwapModuleFactory_PaymentRailsNotContract
├── when the caller is the factory owner
│   ├── it should deploy a new CowSwapModule contract
│   ├── it should set the owner on the deployed module
│   ├── it should wire the module to the PaymentRails
│   ├── it should deploy to the predicted address
│   ├── it should register the module in the factory
│   └── it should emit a CowSwapModuleCreated event
├── when the same salt is reused with the same params
│   └── it should revert
├── when different salts are used
│   └── it should deploy to different addresses
├── when the same salt is used with different owners
│   └── it should deploy to different addresses
├── when the same salt is used with different paymentRails
│   └── it should deploy to different addresses
└── when fuzzing the prediction
    └── it should match the deployed address
